1
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Prepare for an unforgettable trip.

2
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Luca is a animation, comedy, fantasy film directed by Enrico Casarosa.

3
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Luca and his best friend Alberto experience an
unforgettable summer on the Italian Riviera.

4
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:46,000
But all the fun is threatened by a deeply-held secret: they are sea
monsters from another world just below the water’s surface.

5
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:56,000
Luca Paguro (voice), played by Jacob Tremblay.

6
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Alberto Scorfano (voice), played by Jack Dylan Grazer.

7
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:16,000
Giulia Marcovaldo (voice), played by Emma Berman.

8
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:26,000
Ercole Visconti (voice), played by Saverio Raimondo.

9
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Daniela Paguro (voice), played by Maya Rudolph.

10
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Massimo Marcovaldo (voice), played by Marco Barricelli.

11
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:56,000
Luca is a 2021 American animated fantasy film produced by
Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures.

12
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
The film was directed by Enrico Casarosa, produced by Andrea Warren and written by Jesse Andrews
and Mike Jones from a story developed by Casarosa, Andrews, and Simon Stephenson.

13
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:16,000
It stars the voices of Jacob Tremblay, Jack Dylan Grazer, Emma Berman, Saverio
Raimondo, Maya Rudolph, Marco Barricelli, and Jim Gaffigan.

14
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:26,000
The film is set on the Italian Riviera in the 1950s, and centers on Luca Paguro (Tremblay), a young sea monster boy with the ability to assume human form while on land, who
explores the town of Portorosso with his new best friends, Alberto Scorfano (Grazer) and Giulia Marcovaldo (Berman), experiencing a life-changing summer adventure.

15
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Luca draws inspiration from Casarosa's childhood in Genoa, Italy.

16
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Several Pixar artists were sent to the Italian Riviera gathering research from
Italian culture and environment to create Portorosso, the primary setting.

17
00:53:50,000 --> 00:53:56,000
The sea monsters, a "metaphor for feeling different", were loosely
based on old Italian regional myths and folklore.

18
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
As with the short film La Luna (2011), the design and animation were inspired
by hand-drawn and stop motion works and Hayao Miyazaki's style.

19
01:00:10,000 --> 01:00:16,000
Casarosa described the result as a film that "pays homage to Federico Fellini and other
classic Italian filmmakers, with a dash of Miyazaki in the mix too".

20
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Development on Luca lasted for five years, with production
being done remotely during the COVID-19 pandemic.

21
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
Dan Romer composed the film's musical score.

22
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
Luca premiered at the Aquarium of Genoa on June 13, 2021, and was released direct-to-streaming on
Disney+ in the United States on June 18, 2021 in response to the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic.

23
01:12:50,000 --> 01:12:56,000
It was released in theaters in countries without the streaming service, and given a simultaneous
one-week theatrical run at Hollywood's El Capitan Theatre, from June 18 to 24, 2021.

24
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
It was theatrically released in the United States on March 22, 2024.

25
01:19:10,000 --> 01:19:16,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, and was the most-viewed
streaming film of 2021, with over 10.6 billion minutes watched.

26
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
It was nominated for Best Animated Feature Film at the 79th
Golden Globe Awards and the 94th Academy Awards.

27
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
A short film, Ciao Alberto, was released on Disney+ on November 12, 2021.

28
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
The film explores themes of friendship, monster, italy, villain, coming of age.

29
01:31:50,000 --> 01:31:56,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
